    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τᾱγ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταγός</span> or <i>chief</i> of
			Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				6.1.19
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be united under one</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταγός</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				6.1.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be chief of a phratria,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Schwyzer
				323
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>B</u>
				31
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				33
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>to be magistrate</i> of a Thessalian town, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).517.24
			</span></i> (Larissa, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				531.2
			</span></i> (Thess., <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>let</i> soldiers <i>be posted</i> or
				<i>stationed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας ἀρίστους . . πυλῶν ἐπ᾽
					ἐξόδοισι τάγευσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					58
				</span></i>
			.</div>
